### FieldLens API — Auth flow demo
### Day 3 acceptance criteria: register → login → protected route →
### refresh → revoke, demonstrable in this file.
###
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (by Huachao Mao).
### Server must be running first: npm run dev
###
### Click the "Send Request" link that appears above each block below,
### in order, top to bottom. Tokens are captured automatically from each
### response and reused in later requests — no manual copy-paste needed.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:3000

### 1. Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Demo User",
  "email": "demo@fieldlens.dev",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Login as the field worker — capture tokens for later steps
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@fieldlens.dev",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Access a protected route with the access token from step 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4. Admin-only route with a FIELD_WORKER token — expect 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/admin-test
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Login as the seeded admin — capture a separate admin token
# @name adminLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@fieldlens.dev",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 6. Admin-only route with an ADMIN token — expect 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/admin-test
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 7. Refresh — exchange the field worker's refresh token for a new pair
# @name refreshed
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 8. Logout — revoke the NEW refresh token from step 7
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshed.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}

### 9. Confirm revocation — reusing the same refresh token should now fail
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshed.response.body.refreshToken}}"
}
